title: The First of April
subtitle: The Zentrale must decide whether to go on.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: crisis_march = 1 and crisis_time = 3 and e21_ma_calloff = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
on-arrival: {!
var r = Q.e21_ma_out / Q.e21_ma_need;
Q.e21_ma_state = (r >= 0.8) ? 1 : ((r >= 0.45) ? 2 : 3);
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Out on strike: about ' + Math.round(Q.e21_ma_out / 10) * 10 + ',000 of the ' + Q.e21_ma_need + ',000 it takes';
Q.crisis_line_2 = ['Leuna: occupied by its workers', 'Leuna: held against the police', 'Leuna: stormed on 29 March', 'Leuna: given up without a fight'][Q.e21_leuna];
Q.crisis_line_3 = (Q.e21_ma_rift >= 5) ? 'At the gates: the other workers have turned on us' : ((Q.e21_ma_rift >= 3) ? 'At the gates: worker against worker' : (Q.e21_ma_rift ? 'At the gates: some fights with the men at work' : 'At the gates: no fights yet'));
!}

= The First of April

[? if e21_ma_state = 1 : The line is holding. In Berlin and the Ruhr the strike is growing instead of shrinking, and Hörsing is asking for the Reichswehr. General von Seeckt is asking for written orders. ?][? if e21_ma_state = 2 : Nothing is decided. The strike holds in Central Germany and in a few other places. Every day it lasts, the police take more of our people. ?][? if e21_ma_state = 3 : The action is collapsing. Outside Central Germany the call has been ignored, and thousands are in prison. ?][? if e21_ma_rift >= 3 : In some towns the men who stayed at work have beaten our pickets, and in others our pickets have beaten them. ?]

[? if e21_ma_eberlein = 1 : The police have found the detonators from Eberlein's bombs, and are following the trail to Berlin. ?]

- @calloff: Call off the action.
- @fight: Fight on for another week.
- @retreat: Send the men home, and keep the rifles.

@calloff
subtitle: Saves what can still be saved.
on-arrival: e21_ma_calloff = 1; lean_luxemburgist += 1; lean_unionist += 1

The order goes out to the districts by courier: back to work, together, and hide the arms.

@fight
subtitle: One more week, and perhaps the country will move. The pickets are getting rougher.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_ma_out += (Q.militancy >= 60) ? 40 : 15;
Q.e21_ma_rift += 1;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    if (Q['district_' + d + '_strike']) { RG.district(d, {repression: 5}); }
}
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Out on strike: about ' + Math.round(Q.e21_ma_out / 10) * 10 + ',000 of the ' + Q.e21_ma_need + ',000 it takes';
Q.crisis_line_2 = ['Leuna: occupied by its workers', 'Leuna: held against the police', 'Leuna: stormed on 29 March', 'Leuna: given up without a fight'][Q.e21_leuna];
Q.crisis_line_3 = (Q.e21_ma_rift >= 5) ? 'At the gates: the other workers have turned on us' : ((Q.e21_ma_rift >= 3) ? 'At the gates: worker against worker' : (Q.e21_ma_rift ? 'At the gates: some fights with the men at work' : 'At the gates: no fights yet'));
!}

The Rote Fahne, printed in secret, tells the districts to hold on.

@retreat
subtitle: A little ground lost now. The fighting groups will still be there next year.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_arms_saved = 1;
Q.e21_ma_out = Math.max(20, Q.e21_ma_out - 20);
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Out on strike: about ' + Math.round(Q.e21_ma_out / 10) * 10 + ',000 of the ' + Q.e21_ma_need + ',000 it takes';
Q.crisis_line_2 = ['Leuna: occupied by its workers', 'Leuna: held against the police', 'Leuna: stormed on 29 March', 'Leuna: given up without a fight'][Q.e21_leuna];
Q.crisis_line_3 = (Q.e21_ma_rift >= 5) ? 'At the gates: the other workers have turned on us' : ((Q.e21_ma_rift >= 3) ? 'At the gates: worker against worker' : (Q.e21_ma_rift ? 'At the gates: some fights with the men at work' : 'At the gates: no fights yet'));
!}

The fighting groups pull back to the villages and bury their rifles. The strike committees stay in being.
